# Line endings are LF, everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, git on Windows checks out CRLF (core.autocrlf defaults to true there),
# and every file a Windows contributor touches comes back with its whole contents marked
# as changed. That buries a two-line fix in a thousand-line diff, and it makes any tool
# that searches for a multi-line pattern -- a codemod, a linter's autofix, sed -- silently
# miss.
#
# The codebase is LF-authored, the servers run Linux, and every editor worth using has
# handled LF on Windows for a decade.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never touches the bytes.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
